Based on my comprehensive analysis, I have identified the exact location where the fix needs to be implemented for the issue "Fixed #6199 -- Show all languages on language chooser if user is staff".

The problem is in the `LanguageChooser.get_context` method in `menus/templatetags/menu_tags.py`, specifically on line 387 where it filters languages with `if lang.get('public', True):`. This condition only shows public languages to all users, but staff users should see all languages.

Here are the locations requiring modification:

```
menus/templatetags/menu_tags.py
function: LanguageChooser.get_context
line: 386
line: 387
line: 388
```

The fix involves modifying the language filtering logic to check if the user is staff (`request.user.is_staff`) and if so, include all languages regardless of their public status. The context already contains the request object, making this check straightforward to implement.
